I've written two task files for this session. The commit step did nothing, because session_plan/ is gitignored. That's harmless: the instruction ended with || true, and both files are on disk.

Task 01: Fixes #1106 (product). Auto-memory currently stops saving once it holds 20 entries: it keeps the oldest and refuses every new one. In this repo it froze on 2026-08-12. Most of its entries are panic headers cut off before the actual error message, and they still go into every system prompt.
• My decision: when the store is full, drop the oldest auto entry instead of the new one, and never drop an entry the user saved with /remember.
• Also: stop saving a panic note that has no message. If the message is available, save its first line instead.
• No prompt cap: a separate cap on what reaches the prompt isn't needed, since the store will always hold the newest 20.
• Existing stores: the task says how stores written before this change get un-frozen. Without that, the frozen store in this repo would stay frozen, which is the bug.
• Tests and size: the task lists tests for a store under the cap, a full store, protected user entries, old stores and the existing dedup. src/memory.rs is 1,807 of 2,000 lines, so new tests go in a sibling file if needed.

Task 02: Fixes #1105 (product, backlog drain). The backlog has 18 open issues, above the threshold of 12, and this one has the least work left. When a deny list is set, list_files will hold back a "Warnings from find" line that was cut short by the 2,000-character limit. Today, a cut that lands inside a denied directory's own name lets that partial name reach the model. With no deny list, output stays byte-identical, and a test pins that. The task also asks for a break-and-restore check on the new test, a docs sentence, the ARCHITECTURE.md entry changed to past tense, and a search for every #1105 reference before the push closes the ticket.

